#
# BusyBox init reads this file. The format is <id>:<runlevels>:<action>:<process>;
# the id names the terminal (empty: the console) and the runlevels are ignored.

# What the boot does is in /etc/init.d/rcS. It runs once and init waits for it.
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS

# A login prompt on the console, started again whenever the session ends. The
# one account is root, with the password that ssh and the panel take too
# (onu-store keeps it; until one is set it is "admin"). The speed stays the
# one the boot loader set, 115200 baud.
console::respawn:/sbin/getty -L console 0 vt100

# What init does when it is told to restart or halt.
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
